{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","commitSha":"c2534ff9c84422e00711da31629a76f3f59feb98","shard":"52799b6b2d8a03de","symbols":[{"path":"xrpl/ValidPseudoAccounts","kind":"class","name":"ValidPseudoAccounts","qualifiedName":"xrpl::ValidPseudoAccounts","scope":"xrpl","category":"production","access":"public","documentation":{"status":"present","brief":[{"type":"text","text":"Invariants: Pseudo-accounts have valid and consistent properties."}],"description":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Pseudo-accounts have certain properties, and some of those properties are unique to pseudo-accounts. Check that all pseudo-accounts are following the rules, and that only pseudo-accounts look like pseudo-accounts."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Post-fixCleanup3_5_0, a pseudo-account also owns only entries that belong to its own AMM, Vault or LoanBroker:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"text","text":"AMM: its AMM entry, its holdings of the two pool assets, and the trust lines of its LP token,"}],[{"type":"text","text":"Vault: its share MPTokenIssuance, its holding of the vault asset, and the LoanBrokers operating on this vault,"}],[{"type":"text","text":"LoanBroker: its Loans and its holding of the vault asset (the cover)."}]]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A pseudo-account cannot sign transactions, so it could never accept or remove any other object linked into its owner directory. Such an object would pin the directory and block deletion of the owning object."}]}],"returns":null,"notes":[],"suppressionReason":null,"inheritedFrom":null},"location":{"declaration":{"file":"include/xrpl/tx/invariants/InvariantCheck.h","line":382},"definition":{"file":"include/xrpl/tx/invariants/InvariantCheck.h","line":383,"endLine":397}},"corrections":[],"templateParameters":null,"isTemplateSpecialization":false,"isFinal":false,"isAbstract":false,"baseClasses":[],"derivedClasses":[],"friends":[],"deductionGuides":[],"ne